    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Every file in this run was processed: move the checkpoint to the newest file's modified time.\nconst state = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nlet latest = state.lastProcessedModified;\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const t = item.json.lastModifiedDateTime;\n  if (t && (!latest || new Date(t) > new Date(latest))) latest = t;\n}\nstate.lastProcessedModified = latest;\nreturn [{ json: { filesProcessed: $input.all().length, lastProcessedModified: latest } }];"
      },
      "id": "e61011b9-ed5a-4ed3-9b09-46cf62820e58",
      "name": "Save checkpoint",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1800,
        520
      ],
      "notes": "Why Code: Remove Duplicates considered. It records files before they're processed, so a failed run would skip them for good. This saves the checkpoint only after every file in the run succeeded."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## TVM tickets: SharePoint HTML → Excel (daily)\n\nEvery day at **13:00** (n8n instance timezone) this lists the **ServiceFabric** source folder, takes every `.html`/`.htm` file modified since the last successful run, turns each one into `tvm-overdue-<date>.xlsx` (same parsing as the form version) and uploads it to the **IPEngineering** folder, overwriting a file with the same name.\n\n### One-time setup\n1. Select your **Microsoft SharePoint OAuth2 API** credential in **List source folder**, **Download HTML** and **Upload Excel**.\n2. **Download HTML**: replace the two ⚠ placeholders: the ServiceFabric **Site**, then the source **Parent Folder**. Leave **File** as it is. *List source folder* reads these two picks, so this is the only place you set the source.\n3. **Upload Excel**: replace the two ⚠ placeholders: the IPEngineering **Site**, then the destination **Parent Folder**.\n4. Import **TVM - Teams failure alert**, set it up and publish it. Then here: **Workflow Settings → Error workflow →** that workflow.\n5. Click **Execute workflow** to test, then publish (activate).\n\nBoth folders must be in their site's default **Documents** (Shared Documents) library. The v1 SharePoint node, the only one your credential works with, can't reach other libraries.\n\n### Config\n- `ownerList`: empty = all owners. Add names to keep only those (the form version's five are in the node's notes).\n- `statusList`: empty = every SLA status. `[\"Overdue\"]` = the old overdue-only output.\n- `lookbackDays`: how far back to look before the first checkpoint exists.\n\n### Re-running a file\nRe-upload or edit the HTML: anything modified after the checkpoint is picked up on the next run. A failed run leaves the checkpoint alone, so the next day retries its files. Manual runs never move the checkpoint.\n",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 660,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "a8ead4b3-67c4-498a-aa68-28cd87a948b0",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        480
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Why \"Next file\" is its own branch\nFor each file, n8n first runs the top branch (Download HTML → … → Upload Excel), because branches run top to bottom. Then **Next file** asks the loop for the next file. If the top branch stops early (e.g. no rows match `ownerList`/`statusList`), the loop still moves on. **Keep Next file below Download HTML on the canvas.**\n\nAfter the last file, **Save checkpoint** runs. If any file fails, the run stops there and the checkpoint stays put, so the next run retries it.\n",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "145f4c31-2301-4154-bda8-cb1d4baba87e",
      "name": "Loop order",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2020,
        240
      ]
    }
  ],
